{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_011CdosownWPYbNu3sR9DoF8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A few things worth weighing:\n\n**Migration cost** — exporting history, preserving links, and keeping old references working. This is often underestimated; broken links in PRs and docs linger for years.\n\n**Workflow fit** — does the new tracker match how your team actually works (board views, custom fields, automation, triage flow)? A mismatch here is more painful than a rough migration.\n\n**Integrations** — CI/CD, Slack, GitHub/GitLab, on-call tools. Check that the things you rely on today are first-class in the new system, not just available via workarounds.\n\n**Search and query power** — teams tend to undervalue this until they lose it. JQL, saved filters, bulk edits — these matter a lot at scale.\n\n**Pricing model** — per-seat vs. flat vs. usage-based; how it scales as the team grows.\n\n**Adoption risk** — switching costs are partly social. If the team is already frustrated with the current tracker, that's tailwind. If they're neutral, the disruption might not be worth it.\n\nThe most common trap: optimizing for the demo experience of the new tool rather than the daily-use experience six months in. What's driving the switch? That'll narrow down what to prioritize."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7827,"cache_read_input_tokens":19604,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7827},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aa5e4e7a-cd5f-4778-aeb8-4afae216cff3","uuid":"6d5e6f8c-ce89-491a-83ff-2f1e0c8a03d3","timestamp":"2026-08-07T18:40:17.246Z","request_id":"req_011CdosovRQJNBS7zYjuqPKD"}
